[h1]Spire Mentor: beta[/h1]

[b]Beta build of Spire Mentor, for testing.[/b] Unsubscribe from the [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3821016481]regular Spire Mentor item[/url] while this one is installed: the game loads only one mod per id. Everything the regular item does, this one does too; its page has the full description, keys and settings.

[h2]New in this beta (0.11.3-beta.1)[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Game v0.113.0 is simulated exactly[/b] for Ironclad, Silent, Defect, Regent and Necrobinder, so the advice there is no longer approximate. The Fool's cards that show up in other characters' runs (Splash, Colorful Philosophers and the like) are simulated too. Runs as The Fool still get no advice.
[*][b]Stronger Instinct[/b]: new weights that win 73% of Ironclad A10 test runs, up from 57%.
[*][b]Instinct's win estimate leads the advice panel[/b]: "Run 71% · Fight 100%", colored green, amber or red, with the HP this fight is expected to cost. Both numbers assume Instinct plays every move from here. The [b]Show win bar[/b] setting turns it off.
[*][b]AI partners and co-op lobbies work on v0.113.0[/b]. Partners used to fail to join there. Co-op Blitz lobbies work too.
[*][b]Instinct in Blitz shops[/b]: it no longer leaves the merchant without buying. Blitz wares now go through the same simple rule as the other brains.
[*][b]Fixes[/b]: AI partners no longer try card picks the game refuses, such as enchanting a card that cannot take the enchantment. Autopilot no longer reads a stale hand while a card's selection is still open. It no longer gets stuck at the next act's Ancient because the map still offered the previous act's rooms.
[/list]
Everything else is the regular item's 0.11.2.

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Windows only.[/b] The AI runs as a bundled Windows program (SimAdvisor.exe). On Mac or Linux the mod loads but the coach cannot start.
[*][b]Game builds v0.107.1, v0.111.0 and v0.113.0 (public beta; no The Fool yet).[/b] A game update can break the mod until a new version is out.
[*][b]BaseLib[/b] (by Alchyr), which Steam installs alongside this mod as a required item.
[/list]

[h2]Reporting a bug[/h2]
Press [b]Ctrl+Shift+B[/b] (or [b]Panels → Report a bug[/b]) the moment something goes wrong, say what happened in one line, and press [b]Send report[/b]. Nothing is sent until you press Send. Paste the link it puts on your clipboard into a comment here or a GitHub issue.

